1
00:00:00,442 --> 00:00:03,112
(Howard:)Professor,
can you identify our cricket?

2
00:00:03,278 --> 00:00:04,318
(Prof Crawley:)Of course I can.

3
00:00:04,488 --> 00:00:08,238
(Prof Crawley:)I can identify every insect
and arachnid on the planet.

4
00:00:08,408 --> 00:00:11,698
Not that that's gonna keep me from
having to move in with my daughter...

5
00:00:11,870 --> 00:00:17,040
(Prof Crawley:)...in Oxnard. And we're not talking
Oxnard at the beach. No.

6
00:00:17,209 --> 00:00:21,299
(Prof Crawley:)We're talking Oxnard
in the onion fields.

7
00:00:24,675 --> 00:00:28,055
(Howard:)-Well, could you look at Toby?
-Toby?

8
00:00:29,638 --> 00:00:32,138
(Prof Crawley:)What a stupid name for a cricket.

9
00:00:33,517 --> 00:00:35,147
(Sheldon:)Told you.

10
00:00:35,811 --> 00:00:36,851
(Prof Crawley:)It's a field cricket.

11
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:38,100
(Howard:)-Yes.
-No, wait.

12
00:00:38,271 --> 00:00:40,021
(Sheldon:)Dr. Crawley, are you sure?

13
00:00:40,190 --> 00:00:43,820
(Prof Crawley:)Young man, I've been studying insects
since I was 8 years old.

14
00:00:43,986 --> 00:00:46,826
(Prof Crawley:)You know what they used to call me
in school?

15
00:00:46,989 --> 00:00:48,779
(Prof Crawley:)Creepy Crawley.

16
00:00:49,616 --> 00:00:52,706
(Sheldon:)Cruel as that may be,
that is not in itself a credential.

17
00:00:54,579 --> 00:00:55,999
(Prof Crawley:)Let me show you something.

18
00:00:56,873 --> 00:01:00,023
(Prof Crawley:)See that?
That's a Crawley's dung beetle.

